# Plan: Geo-tiered CTA mode toggle — settings-based buy/trial swap at hydrate level

## Summary

Add a `ctaMode` settings flag (values: `default`, `buy-only`, `trial-only`) per geo/surface that suppresses conflicting CTAs at hydrate time in `web-components`. The toggle is authored in Studio and delivered through the existing MAS-IO settings pipeline — no card fragment content is modified. When a card's only CTA conflicts with the active mode and no paired CTA exists, a Learn More fallback link is rendered instead.

## Task Description

On a per-locale/surface basis, GTM admins must be able to set `ctaMode` in Studio settings. The IO settings transformer delivers this flag in the fragment settings payload. During hydration in `web-components/src/hydrate.js`, `processCTAs` reads `settings.ctaMode` and:
- `buy-only`: hides CTAs with `data-modal="twp"` (trial), shows `data-modal="d2p"` (buy)
- `trial-only`: hides CTAs with `data-modal="d2p"` (buy), shows `data-modal="twp"` (trial)
- `default`: no change (existing behavior)

Suppressed CTAs are fully removed from the DOM (not just visually hidden). Single-CTA cards that conflict fall back to a `learnMoreUrl` anchor. A new `learnMoreUrl` field is added to the settings model for use as the fallback.

## Relevant Files

| File | Action | Reason |
|------|--------|--------|
| `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js` | Edit | Add `ctaMode` and `learnMoreUrl` to `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` |
| `web-components/src/hydrate.js` | Edit | Add `processCtaMode()` function; call from `hydrate()` before `processCTAs` |
| `web-components/src/constants.js` | Edit | Export `CTA_MODE` constant object (`DEFAULT`, `BUY_ONLY`, `TRIAL_ONLY`) |
| `studio/src/settings/setting-name-map.js` | Edit | No change needed — auto-derives from `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` import |
| `studio/src/settings/mas-settings.js` | Read/Verify | Confirm `ctaMode` select editor renders from `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` |
| `web-components/test/unit/hydrate.test.js` | Edit | Add unit tests for `processCtaMode` |
| `io/www/test/fragment/transformers/settings.test.js` | Edit | Add test for `ctaMode` extraction |

## Step by Step Tasks

### 1. Add `CTA_MODE` constants to `web-components/src/constants.js`

- Add export:
  ```js
  export const CTA_MODE = {
      DEFAULT: 'default',
      BUY_ONLY: 'buy-only',
      TRIAL_ONLY: 'trial-only',
  };
  ```
- Validate: `node --check web-components/src/constants.js`

### 2. Register `ctaMode` and `learnMoreUrl` in the settings transformer

- In `io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js`, append to `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS`:
  ```js
  { name: 'ctaMode', valueType: 'text', editor: 'select' },
  { name: 'learnMoreUrl', valueType: 'text', editor: 'text' },
  ```
- `ctaMode` is a plain text field carrying one of the three CTA_MODE values; no special `propertyName` needed.
- `learnMoreUrl` is a plain text URL stored as-is.
- Validate: `node --check io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js`

### 3. Implement `processCtaMode` in `web-components/src/hydrate.js`

- Import `CTA_MODE` and `MODAL_TYPE_3_IN_1` from `./constants.js`.
- Add function before `processCTAs`:

  ```js
  /**
   * Suppresses CTAs that conflict with the active ctaMode setting.
   * Fully removes conflicting CTAs from the DOM; falls back to a
   * Learn More anchor if no compatible CTA remains.
   * @param {object} fields - fragment fields
   * @param {object} settings - resolved settings (may include ctaMode, learnMoreUrl)
   */
  export function processCtaMode(fields, settings) {
      const mode = settings?.ctaMode;
      if (!mode || mode === CTA_MODE.DEFAULT) return;

      const ctas = fields.ctas;
      if (!ctas) return;

      // Parse the CTAs HTML string into a temporary container
      const container = document.createElement('div');
      container.innerHTML = ctas;

      const links = [...container.querySelectorAll('a')];
      if (!links.length) return;

      const suppressModalType =
          mode === CTA_MODE.BUY_ONLY
              ? MODAL_TYPE_3_IN_1.TWP  // suppress trial CTAs
              : MODAL_TYPE_3_IN_1.D2P; // suppress buy CTAs

      links.forEach((link) => {
          if (link.dataset.modal === suppressModalType) {
              link.remove();
          }
      });

      // If no compatible CTAs remain after suppression, use Learn More fallback
      const remaining = container.querySelectorAll('a');
      if (!remaining.length) {
          const fallbackUrl = settings?.learnMoreUrl;
          if (fallbackUrl) {
              const learnMore = createTag('a', { href: fallbackUrl, class: 'secondary-link' }, 'Learn More');
              container.append(learnMore);
          } else {
              // No fallback configured — leave fields.ctas empty (no CTA rendered)
              fields.ctas = '';
              return;
          }
      }

      fields.ctas = container.innerHTML;
  }
  ```

- In the `hydrate()` function, call `processCtaMode(fields, settings)` immediately before `processCTAs(fields, merchCard, mapping, variant)` (line 829):
  ```js
  processCtaMode(fields, settings);
  processCTAs(fields, merchCard, mapping, variant);
  ```

- Validate: `node --check web-components/src/hydrate.js`

### 4. Add unit tests for `processCtaMode`

- In `web-components/test/unit/hydrate.test.js`, add test suite covering:
  - `default` mode: fields.ctas unchanged
  - `buy-only`: TWP link removed, D2P link retained
  - `trial-only`: D2P link removed, TWP link retained
  - Dual CTAs — both modes — correct one retained
  - Single conflicting CTA with `learnMoreUrl` → replaced by Learn More anchor
  - Single conflicting CTA without `learnMoreUrl` → `fields.ctas` set to `''`
  - No `data-modal` attribute on CTAs → no change (pass-through)

### 5. Add settings transformer test for `ctaMode`

- In `io/www/test/fragment/transformers/settings.test.js` (or equivalent), add a test that:
  - Constructs a settings fragment with a `ctaMode` entry set to `buy-only`
  - Runs through `collectSettingEntries` + `applySettings`
  - Asserts `fragment.settings.ctaMode === 'buy-only'`

### 6. Verify Studio settings UI renders the new fields

- Read `studio/src/settings/mas-settings.js` `renderSettingEditor()` method to confirm a `select` editor type is handled for `ctaMode`.
- If `select` editor type is not handled, add a `case 'select':` rendering a `<sp-picker>` or equivalent with options `default`, `buy-only`, `trial-only` in the existing switch/if-else editor renderer.
- Read `studio/src/settings/mas-setting-item.js` to confirm override dialog handles text editor for `learnMoreUrl`.

## Acceptance Criteria

- `settings.ctaMode = 'buy-only'` causes all fragments whose `fields.ctas` contains a `data-modal="twp"` link to have that link removed from the rendered CTA slot before mount
- `settings.ctaMode = 'trial-only'` causes all fragments whose `fields.ctas` contains a `data-modal="d2p"` link to have that link removed before mount
- When the only CTA in a card conflicts with the active mode and `settings.learnMoreUrl` is set, a `<a href="{learnMoreUrl}" class="secondary-link">Learn More</a>` is rendered in the CTA slot instead
- When the only CTA conflicts and no `learnMoreUrl` is set, `fields.ctas` is empty and no CTA is rendered (no empty container)
- `settings.ctaMode = 'default'` (or absent) leaves all CTAs unchanged — existing behavior is preserved
- No content fragment data is written; the swap is purely a runtime mutation of `fields.ctas` before `processCTAs` is called
- `SETTING_NAME_DEFINITIONS` in `settings.js` includes both `ctaMode` and `learnMoreUrl` entries, making them available to the Studio settings table automatically
- `node --check` passes on all modified JS files
- All new unit tests pass under `npm run test:ci` in both `io/www` and `web-components`

## Validation Commands

```sh
node --check web-components/src/constants.js
node --check web-components/src/hydrate.js
node --check io/www/src/fragment/transformers/settings.js
cd web-components && npm run test:ci
cd io/www && npm run test:ci
```

